From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com> [Pocknix port]
Subject: [PATCH] input: qcom-hv-haptics: stop zero-amplitude effects immediately

Pocknix port of the ArmadaOS patch
`1004-input-haptics-stop-zero-amplitude-immediately.patch`
(armada-os/armada, packages/kernel/patches/, commit ce363b8e67cfd2b5fcf44fd384686f85d777ae9d).
Fetched raw from
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/armada-os/armada/ce363b8e67cfd2b5fcf44fd384686f85d777ae9d/packages/kernel/patches/1004-input-haptics-stop-zero-amplitude-immediately.patch

WHY THE RENUMBERING
-------------------
ArmadaOS numbers its patch set independently of ours and the numbers collide:
armada `1004` is this haptics fix, while OUR `1004` is
`1004-input-qcom-hv-haptics-defer-rsinput-playback.patch` (ROCKNIX's
rsinput-playback deferral, part of the synced base). Filed here as `2107-`,
sorting after the whole 20-sm8750 stack, with the provenance in the name. Both
patch drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c, so order matters: this sorts after
`2101` (the armada-1003 serialization port) and applies on top of it.

WHAT THE BUG WAS
----------------
ROCKNIX's periodic-sine compatibility patch (our synced base
`1001-haptics-driver-support-periodic-sine-and-fixes.patch`) handled a
zero-amplitude update while the chip was already playing by dropping the gain
to 1 and scheduling a stop five seconds later. Stopping applies the configured
brake pattern, so an ordinary rumble ended in a small but distinct tap exactly
five seconds after it should have gone silent.

Erase the active effect immediately instead, and ignore a following playback
request when no effect is loaded, so a client that sends play right after a
zero-amplitude update cannot restart stale motor state. In-place gain updates
now balance their transient runtime-PM reference with
haptics_runtime_autosuspend_put().

RELATION TO THE 2026-10-16 DRY POWER-OFF
----------------------------------------
This is the second half of the rumble-stop story beside `2101`. On the Odin 3
the last haptics activity before the hardware cut was a stopped-play handshake
("poll HPWR_DISABLED failed after stopped play"); the stop path this patch
touches is exactly the one that runs there, and the delayed brake tap is the
extra motor activity seen around rumble stop. It is not by itself the cause of
the dry power-off (the pstore/ramoops was empty and there was no oops/panic),
but removing the five-second deferred stop and the stale-state restart makes
the rumble-stop path do strictly less work, so it is landed as part of the fix.

ADAPTATION
----------
Verbatim: the ArmadaOS hunks apply to our patched tree (the pinned source + the
full 20-sm8750 stack, which already carries 1000/1001/1004/2101) with ZERO fuzz.
As with our `2102` port only the hunk headers were moved to our tree's line
numbers so the patch also lands at ZERO offset (the ArmadaOS headers were 12
lines early); the added/removed lines are ArmadaOS' byte for byte and the
function names in the hunk headers are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
--- a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
@@ -3205,6 +3205,8 @@ static void haptics_runtime_autosuspend(struct haptics_chip *chip)
 	pm_runtime_autosuspend(chip->dev);
 }
 
+static int haptics_erase(struct input_dev *dev, int effect_id);
+
 static int haptics_upload_effect(struct input_dev *dev,
 		struct ff_effect *effect, struct ff_effect *old);
 
@@ -3266,16 +3268,8 @@ static int haptics_upload_effect(struct input_dev *dev,
 		pr_debug("tried to upload an effect while the chip was busy playing, setting gain...\n");
 
 		if (gain == 0) {
-			//The purpose of scheduling a stop_work work is that if the program calls playback afterwards, it will play
-			// for a very short time using the previous gain
-			// ( Like Aethersx2, it likes to call playback with zero value EVEN when amplitude is zero)
-			//We cant stop the playback now, so schedule rumble stop after 5s
-			//and set the gain to a low value (essentially zero)
-
-			dev_dbg(chip->dev, "scheduling stop after 500ms, because gain is zero\n");
-
-			dev->ff->set_gain(dev, 1);
-			schedule_delayed_work(&chip->stop_work, msecs_to_jiffies(5000));
+			haptics_runtime_autosuspend_put(chip);
+			return haptics_erase(dev, effect->id);
 		} else {
 			dev_dbg(chip->dev, "Setting gain to %hu...\n", gain);
 
@@ -3285,6 +3279,7 @@ static int haptics_upload_effect(struct input_dev *dev,
 			schedule_delayed_work(&chip->stop_work, msecs_to_jiffies(effect->replay.length));
 		}
 
+		haptics_runtime_autosuspend_put(chip);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
@@ -3389,8 +3384,10 @@ static int haptics_playback(struct input_dev *dev, int effect_id, int val)
 
 	dev_dbg(chip->dev, "playback val = %d\n", val);
 	if (!!val && !chip->chip_is_playing) {
-		if (!chip->chip_effect_loaded)
-			dev_warn(chip->dev, "Trying to playback while no effect is loaded!\n");
+		if (!chip->chip_effect_loaded) {
+			dev_dbg(chip->dev, "Trying to playback while no effect is loaded!\n");
+			return 0;
+		}
 
 		if (chip->config.measure_lra_impedance && chip->visense_enabled)
 			chip->pattern_start_time = ktime_get_boottime();
